      "content": "yo, so i had the weirdest thing happen today. i was watching the tech stocks during that sudden dip around 2pm and i literally felt this massive spike in my heart rate right before the sell off started. it was like my body knew the volatility was coming seconds before the tickers actually moved. has anyone ever talked about how physical sensations might actually sync up with market swings? like some kind of bio-rhythm thing?",
